Name the view, the storage and the appearance, because three identical text stacks look alike.

iA Writer builds THREE complete editor stacks, view plus clip view plus layout manager plus text
storage, and puts all three in the window. The document lands in the third and only the first is
ever drawn, so the editor pane stays empty (#194). Nothing in the existing traces could tell the
three apart:

  CIDER_LM container=... setLayoutManager=...     always said textView=nil, because a container is
                                                  bound to its layout manager BEFORE the view exists
  CIDER_TEXTDRAW ...                              only prints for a view that DRAWS, and two of the
                                                  three never do
  CIDER_VIEW viewDidLoad ...                      loads were traced and appearances were NOT, so a
                                                  run showed 50 loads and 0 appearances and READ as
                                                  "the appearance never happened"

Three additions, all under switches that already exist:

  NSTextContainer setTextView:   CIDER_LM setTextView=<ptr>(<class>) container= lm= storage= len=
                                 the only point where a view and its storage are both known.
  NSClipView setDocumentView:    CIDER_DOCVIEW clip= was=<ptr>(<class>) now=<ptr>(<class>)
                                 which view became scrollable, and what it replaced. An application
                                 that swaps editors this way leaves no other trace: the outgoing
                                 view is simply never drawn again, which looks identical to a view
                                 that was never installed.
  NSViewController appearance    CIDER_VIEW viewDidAppear/viewDidDisappear <class> view= window=

WHAT THEY MEASURED IMMEDIATELY, in one drive that clicks a file row:

  setTextView=0x...183400(IAEditorTextView) storage=0x...4c4920   <- the only one DRAWN, len 0
  setTextView=0x...229c00(IAEditorTextView) storage=0x...b6400
  setTextView=0x...12f200(IAEditorTextView) storage=0x...b2c40    <- gets the 40 byte document
  CIDER_DOCVIEW clip=... was=(nil) now=...(IAEditorTextView)      three times, three CLIP VIEWS
  CIDER_VIEW viewDidAppear IAEditorViewController ... window=yes  all three, and ZERO disappears

The appearance trace corrected a reading I had already made from its absence, which is the reason
it is here: an instrument that traces one half of a pair turns silence into a false negative.
